        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Margulies\n- Products: Alka-Seltzer\n- Roles: writer, philosopher, advertising-industry creative director\n- Topics: advertising jingles\n\nFacts:\n- Alka-Seltzer was launched in 1931.\n- Alka-Seltzer is an effervescent antacid and pain reliever that was first marketed by the Dr. Miles Medicine Company of Elkhart, Indiana, United States.\n- Paul Eli Margulies was an American writer, philosopher, and advertising-industry creative director who lived from 1935 to 2014.\n- Paul Margulies was famous for writing advertising jingles, including “Plop, Plop, Fizz, Fizz, Oh What a Relief it Is!”",
